<section id="S4.SS2.SSS2" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">4.2.2 </span>Robustness under Interaction Noise.</h4>

<div id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To assess whether <span id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Agent-Reflex</span> remains effective when tool feedback or user interactions are perturbed, we evaluate it on AgentNoiseBench. In detail, every foundation model degrades markedly.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Generalization of <span id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Agent-Reflex</span> to Unseen Perturbations.</span>
Table <a href="#S4.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 4.2.1 Results on Long-Horizon Tool Use. ‣ 4.2 Main Results ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Agent-Reflex:Teaching Language Agents to Act Reflectively" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> shows that <span id="S4.SS2.SSS2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Agent-Reflex</span> achieves the highest Overall score among the compared 8B methods, reaching 29.1% compared with 25.9% for NoisyAgent-8B and outperforming the other strong baselines overall. These results indicate that its effectiveness extends to noisy interaction. Appendix <a href="#A5.SS1" title="E.1 Does Agent-Reflex Act Reflectively Under Noise? ‣ Appendix E Supplement Experimental Results ‣ Agent-Reflex:Teaching Language Agents to Act Reflectively" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">E.1</span></a> provides a fine-grained attribution of the observed noise-robustness gains.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.F4" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2610.17953v1/Agent-Reflex_algorithm_comparison_vector.svg" id="S4.F4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/161;" width="476" height="161"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S4.F4.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 4</span>: </span><span id="S4.F4.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Comparison of agent policy optimization algorithms.<span id="S4.F4.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> All runs start from Qwen3-8B and train for 100 RL steps on the same task pool under matched budgets. </span>(a)<span id="S4.F4.7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Final accuracy on held-out benchmarks. </span>(b)<span id="S4.F4.7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> Mean training reward on the same tasks.</span></span></figcaption>
