<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">5 </span>Conclusion</h2>

<div id="S5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this paper, we present <span id="S5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Agent-Reflex</span>, a general training framework for incentivizing proactive reflective thinking in agents. In detail, <span id="S5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">RSD</span> mines reusable reflection meta-skills from matched success–failure trajectories under grounded tool-feedback perturbations. Building on this skill library, <span id="S5.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">ReSFT</span> turns each skill into complementary supervision for self-reflection, skill recovery, and user-centric correction, and ORPO further elicits proactive reflection by combining agentic reinforcement learning under noisy interaction with reflection-guided on-policy distillation. Across six challenging agent benchmark suites, <span id="S5.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Agent-Reflex</span> improves long-horizon tool use and robustness under tool and user noise with stable training dynamics, supporting scalable agent training.</p>
</div>
</section>
